  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equipping the Namibian national rhino program with a new wildlife veterinarian field vehicle</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to respond to more efficiently and rapidly provide emergency veterinary care for black and white rhinos in northern Namibia, the country&apos;s wildlife authority will be posting a veterinary team in Etosha National Park. This grant will support the purchase and customization of a four-wheel drive vehicle for the veterinary team, equipped with all the necessary equipment for rhino capture for ear-notching, dehorning, implant of tracking devices, DNA sampling, capture and translocation of rhinos out of risky areas, and emergency veterinary care for injured rhinos.</narrative>
  </description>
